1.7 Design patterns
- Provider registry for couriers (providerRegistry.ts) and payment gateways (modules/payments/application.ts)
- Repository pattern: prismaInventoryRepository, prismaAccountingRepository, prismaPaymentRepository
- Service modules with contracts (modules/*/contracts.ts)
- Domain events (decorative — console-only, no subscribers)
- Singleton services: Redis (ensureRedis), Prisma, queue map
- AsyncLocalStorage tenant context via Prisma $extends (dormant — see §16)
1.8 Coding style & naming
- TypeScript ESM ("type":"module"), Prettier (semi, singleQuote, printWidth:120), ESLint flat config
- Screens use kebab-case filenames (HomePage.tsx); exported components PascalCase; any heavily used (~100s of warnings); heavy any-casting in server.ts
- No TODO/FIXME/HACK markers in src/** (verified clean — but also no @ts-ignore, unusual for 17k lines)
1.9 Authentication strategy
Custom: email/password (bcrypt) + Supabase OAuth. JWT access token (role-scoped TTL: 24h customer, 1h privileged) + rotating refresh token, both in httpOnly cookies + Redis-backed session store (sessionStore.ts:96-135). Supabase only used for OAuth identity exchange (/api/auth/supabase/exchange); the local User table is the source of truth. Phone OTP + email verification exist (tokens in DB). 2FA flag exists on schema but no flow uses it.
1.10 Authorization strategy
- API: authenticateToken + requireRole("...") middlewares (server.ts), or requireUser/requireRole/requirePermission + secureApiRoute for App Router routes
- Pages: requireDashboardAccess(allowedRoles, path) server-side in dashboard layouts + client-side re-check in DashboardLayout.tsx
- RBAC module: modules/rbac/ with can(role, permission) matrix
- Critical gap: secureApiRoute is used only by App Router routes; most Express inline routes do manual req.user checks. CSRF middleware exists (csrf.ts) but is never mounted (see §18).
1.11 State management
- React Contexts: UserProvider > WishlistProvider > CompareProvider > CartProvider > InventoryProvider (AppProviders.tsx)
- Cart stored in Redis server-side (userCartKey(userId)) + client context; wishlist guest→user merge; compare limited to 4
- Custom toast system (lib/toast.tsx, 461 lines) replacing react-hot-toast
